      "side": 1,
      "message": "You\u0027re right it is overloaded now. \n\nOriginally the intent was to avoid the hanging of terminal in agentic/CI contexts. Problem was that pre-upload only had two modes \"all\" or \"some\". With the updated changes, we\u0027ll have the following:\n\n* `repo upload` - interactive prompt.\n* `repo upload --fix --yes` - apply all fixups, no prompt.\n* `repo upload --yes` - do not apply fixups (fail on hook failure), no prompt.\n* `repo upload --yes --ignore-hooks` - do not apply fixups (ignore hook failures), no prompt.\n\nUpdated the change to add the --fix flag. Relevant change required in git-repohooks: https://gerrit-review.git.corp.google.com/c/git-repohooks/+/621761.",
